---
const engines = [
  { icon: "plugin-javascript.svg", name: "JavaScript" },
  { icon: "plugin-unity.svg", name: "Unity" },
  { icon: "plugin-unreal.svg", name: "Unreal" },
  { icon: "plugin-godot.svg", name: "Godot" },
];
// The Storylet Studio home. A STANDALONE page (its own header and footer, light-only),
// deliberately outside the Starlight docs chrome. Brand tokens come from
// src/styles/storylets.css; the landing's own classes live in src/styles/landing.css.
//
// Shape, top to bottom: the shared header, a two-column opening (one sentence, one paragraph,
// one button, the split-deck picture), the list of situations, the Board clip, the three
// tools as paragraphs, the downloads as a list, the shared footer. The header, the footer and
// the downloads list come from src/chrome, which is generated from patterkit/site-chrome and is
// never edited here. The Patter site is a script; this page is a hand of cards. They share
// those three and nothing else in structure.
import "../chrome/fonts.css";
import "../styles/storylets.css";
import "../chrome/palette.css";
import "../chrome/chrome.css";
import "../styles/landing.css";
import LandingHeader from "../chrome/LandingHeader.astro";
import LandingFooter from "../chrome/LandingFooter.astro";
import Downloads from "../chrome/Downloads.astro";
// Made with patterkit's recorder (tools/recorder/takes/storyletter-board.mjs): remake, don't edit.
import boardClip from "../assets/clips/storyletter-board.mp4";
import boardPoster from "../assets/clips/storyletter-board.jpg";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/"); // normalise to a trailing slash
const title = "Storylet Studio";
const description =
  "An open toolkit for storylets. Your designers write small pieces of story as cards, each with a rule for when it fits, and your game deals the ones that fit the moment, on Unity, Unreal, Godot, or the web.";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://storylets.dev/" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://storylets.dev/social-card.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1280" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="640" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://storylets.dev/social-card.png" />
    <link rel="icon" href={`${base}favicon.svg`} type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="icon" href={`${base}favicon.ico`} sizes="48x48" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href={`${base}apple-touch-icon.png`} />
    <style>{"body{margin:0}"}</style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="sy-landing">
      <LandingHeader />

      <!-- OPENING -->
      <section class="sy-open">
        <div class="sy-wrap sy-open-grid">
          <div class="sy-open-copy">
            <h1 class="sy-h1">Design your story as cards that decide when they play.</h1>
            <p class="sy-lead">A storylet is a small piece of story with a rule for when it should appear. Your designers write
              them as cards in Storyletter, you drop one file into Unity, Unreal, Godot, or the web, and whenever your
              game needs to pick something, it asks the engine for a hand and gets the cards that fit the moment.</p>
            <div class="sy-actions">
              <a class="chrome-btn sy-btn-primary" href={`${base}getting-started/`}>Get started</a>
              <a class="sy-link" href={`${base}download/`}>Download</a>
            </div>
            <p class="sy-note">It's free and MIT-licensed, and there's no server to run.</p>
          </div>

          {/* One deck, cut on the diagonal: the same six cards as a grid and as a flow. The
              split is the argument the picture makes, so it's one picture rather than two.
              Card faces top-left, the arrows the tool worked out bottom-right. The finish is
              Storyletter's node canvas (packages/studio node-art.ts): white faces with a
              hairline and 6px corners, the deck's colour as a stripe down the left, straight
              edges border to border in the enable and disable inks, named by a key. */}
          <figure class="sy-deck">
            <svg class="sy-both" viewBox="0 0 520 372" role="img" aria-labelledby="sy-both-t">
              <title id="sy-both-t">One deck shown two ways at once, divided on the diagonal. The
                upper half is its cards as a grid, each with the rule for when it comes up. The lower
                half is the same cards as a flow, with arrows the tool worked out from those rules:
                one card opens up another, and shuts a third off.</title>
              <defs>
                <clipPath id="sy-cut-cards"><path d="M0 0 H520 L0 372 Z"></path></clipPath>
                <clipPath id="sy-cut-flow"><path d="M520 0 V372 H0 Z"></path></clipPath>
                {/* The canvas's arrowhead: 9 long, 7 wide, solid, in the edge's own ink. */}
                <marker id="sy-a-on" viewBox="0 0 9 7" refX="9" refY="3.5" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" markerWidth="9" markerHeight="7" orient="auto">
                  <path d="M0 0 L9 3.5 L0 7 z" fill="var(--l-on)"></path>
                </marker>
                <marker id="sy-a-off" viewBox="0 0 9 7" refX="9" refY="3.5" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" markerWidth="9" markerHeight="7" orient="auto">
                  <path d="M0 0 L9 3.5 L0 7 z" fill="var(--l-off)"></path>
                </marker>
                <pattern id="sy-dots" width="16" height="16" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><circle class="sy-dot" cx="8" cy="8" r="0.9"></circle></pattern>
                {/* Each face clipped to its own corners, so the deck stripe follows the curve. */}
                <clipPath id="sy-c1"><rect x="20" y="16" width="128" height="66" rx="6"></rect></clipPath>
                <clipPath id="sy-c2"><rect x="156" y="16" width="128" height="66" rx="6"></rect></clipPath>
                <clipPath id="sy-c3"><rect x="292" y="16" width="128" height="66" rx="6"></rect></clipPath>
                <clipPath id="sy-c4"><rect x="20" y="96" width="128" height="66" rx="6"></rect></clipPath>
                <clipPath id="sy-c5"><rect x="156" y="96" width="128" height="66" rx="6"></rect></clipPath>
                <clipPath id="sy-c6"><rect x="20" y="176" width="128" height="66" rx="6"></rect></clipPath>
                <clipPath id="sy-f1"><rect x="150" y="268" width="160" height="56" rx="6"></rect></clipPath>
                <clipPath id="sy-f2"><rect x="370" y="180" width="140" height="52" rx="6"></rect></clipPath>
                <clipPath id="sy-f3"><rect x="370" y="268" width="140" height="52" rx="6"></rect></clipPath>
              </defs>

              <g clip-path="url(#sy-cut-cards)">
                <g class="sy-gc sy-deck-forge"><rect x="20" y="16" width="128" height="66" rx="6"></rect>
                  <rect class="sy-stripe" clip-path="url(#sy-c1)" x="20" y="16" width="4" height="66"></rect>
                  <text class="sy-gc-t" x="34" y="36">The Blacksmith&apos;s</text>
                  <text class="sy-gc-t" x="34" y="52">Trouble</text>
                  <text class="sy-gc-r" x="34" y="71">when: met Gareth</text></g>
                <g class="sy-gc sy-deck-gareth"><rect x="156" y="16" width="128" height="66" rx="6"></rect>
                  <rect class="sy-stripe" clip-path="url(#sy-c2)" x="156" y="16" width="4" height="66"></rect>
                  <text class="sy-gc-t" x="170" y="36">Gareth Asks</text>
                  <text class="sy-gc-t" x="170" y="52">for Help</text>
                  <text class="sy-gc-r" x="170" y="71">when: he owes you</text></g>
                <g class="sy-gc sy-deck-forge"><rect x="292" y="16" width="128" height="66" rx="6"></rect>
                  <rect class="sy-stripe" clip-path="url(#sy-c3)" x="292" y="16" width="4" height="66"></rect>
                  <text class="sy-gc-t" x="306" y="36">The Ring of</text>
                  <text class="sy-gc-t" x="306" y="52">the Anvil</text>
                  <text class="sy-gc-r" x="306" y="71">when: always</text></g>
                <g class="sy-gc sy-deck-inn"><rect x="20" y="96" width="128" height="66" rx="6"></rect>
                  <rect class="sy-stripe" clip-path="url(#sy-c4)" x="20" y="96" width="4" height="66"></rect>
                  <text class="sy-gc-t" x="34" y="116">A Rumour at</text>
                  <text class="sy-gc-t" x="34" y="132">the Inn</text>
                  <text class="sy-gc-r" x="34" y="151">when: debt called</text></g>
                <g class="sy-gc sy-deck-forge"><rect x="156" y="96" width="128" height="66" rx="6"></rect>
                  <rect class="sy-stripe" clip-path="url(#sy-c5)" x="156" y="96" width="4" height="66"></rect>
                  <text class="sy-gc-t" x="170" y="116">The Forge</text>
                  <text class="sy-gc-t" x="170" y="132">Falls Quiet</text>
                  <text class="sy-gc-r" x="170" y="151">when: debt called</text></g>
                <g class="sy-gc sy-deck-inn"><rect x="20" y="176" width="128" height="66" rx="6"></rect>
                  <rect class="sy-stripe" clip-path="url(#sy-c6)" x="20" y="176" width="4" height="66"></rect>
                  <text class="sy-gc-t" x="34" y="196">Mira Pours</text>
                  <text class="sy-gc-t" x="34" y="212">a Second</text>
                  <text class="sy-gc-r" x="34" y="231">when: evening</text></g>
              </g>

              <g clip-path="url(#sy-cut-flow)">
                {/* Its own ground, the canvas's desk with its dots, so the cards it covers read as
                    tucked underneath rather than as rectangles that failed to draw. */}
                <path class="sy-flow-ground" d="M520 0 V372 H0 Z"></path>
                <path d="M520 0 V372 H0 Z" fill="url(#sy-dots)"></path>
                <path class="sy-fe sy-fe-on" d="M295 268 L379 232" marker-end="url(#sy-a-on)"></path>
                <path class="sy-fe sy-fe-off" d="M310 294 L370 294" marker-end="url(#sy-a-off)"></path>
                <g class="sy-fn sy-fn-sel sy-deck-forge"><rect x="150" y="268" width="160" height="56" rx="6"></rect>
                  <rect class="sy-stripe" clip-path="url(#sy-f1)" x="150" y="268" width="4" height="56"></rect>
                  <text class="sy-fn-t" x="165" y="291">The Blacksmith&apos;s</text>
                  <text class="sy-fn-t" x="165" y="309">Trouble</text></g>
                <g class="sy-fn sy-deck-gareth"><rect x="370" y="180" width="140" height="52" rx="6"></rect>
                  <rect class="sy-stripe" clip-path="url(#sy-f2)" x="370" y="180" width="4" height="52"></rect>
                  <text class="sy-fn-t" x="385" y="202">Gareth Asks</text>
                  <text class="sy-fn-t" x="385" y="220">for Help</text></g>
                <g class="sy-fn sy-deck-forge"><rect x="370" y="268" width="140" height="52" rx="6"></rect>
                  <rect class="sy-stripe" clip-path="url(#sy-f3)" x="370" y="268" width="4" height="52"></rect>
                  <text class="sy-fn-t" x="385" y="290">The Forge</text>
                  <text class="sy-fn-t" x="385" y="308">Falls Quiet</text></g>
                {/* The key, as the canvas names its edges: a short line in each ink and the word. */}
                <g class="sy-key">
                  <path class="sy-fe sy-fe-on" d="M344 352 H362"></path><text x="368" y="355.5">opens up</text>
                  <path class="sy-fe sy-fe-off" d="M428 352 H446"></path><text x="452" y="355.5">shuts off</text>
                </g>
              </g>
              <path class="sy-seam" d="M520 0 L0 372"></path>
            </svg>
            <figcaption class="sy-deck-caption">A story made up of cards, each with a rule. The tool works out how
              the story flows as you play.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- WHERE YOU'D USE IT -->
      <section class="sy-uses">
        <div class="sy-wrap">
          <h2 class="sy-h2">Where you'd use it</h2>
          <p class="sy-uses-lead">Anywhere your game has to pick from a pool of possibilities, that's a box of cards.
            There's more on what it's for on the <a href={`${base}why/`}>Why Storylet Studio</a> page.</p>
          <ul class="sy-uses-list">
            <li>Pick which scene of your story plays next.</li>
            <li>Choose the topics an NPC has to talk about.</li>
            <li>Spawn the encounter that fits this spot on the map.</li>
            <li>Decide which items turn up to be picked up.</li>
            <li>Offer the player a quest or a job.</li>
            <li>Work out who's in town today.</li>
            <li>Pick the bark line that fits right now (though <a href="https://patterkit.dev">Patter</a> is the better tool for barks).</li>
            <li>Choose the lore that appears in the player's codex.</li>
            <li>Give an actor at an immersive event the topic to raise with a visitor.</li>
            <li>Send a visitor on to the next room of an interactive event.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- THE BOARD -->
      <section class="sy-board">
        <div class="sy-wrap sy-board-grid">
          <div class="sy-board-copy">
            <h2 class="sy-h2">Watch a hand get dealt</h2>
            <p>Press Play in Storyletter and the Board deals turn by turn, laying each hand out under its name, or on
              the map where it stands, so you can see what the engine picked and what it left in the box. The journal down the side
              records every deal and play and what each one changed, and a peek in the State tab lists the cards
              a deal passes over and why, so "why didn't that happen?" has an answer you can read.</p>
          </div>
          <video class="sy-board-shot" src={boardClip} poster={boardPoster.src} width="1280" height="800" autoplay muted loop playsinline aria-label="The Board in Storyletter playing The Village on its illustrated map. A card at the Elder's House is opened, read and played, and cards are dealt into every region of the map at once as the journal fills down the side. Then the view goes down into the caves and plays one of the cards waiting there."></video>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- THE TOOLS -->
      <section id="tools" class="sy-tools">
        <div class="sy-wrap sy-tools-inner">
          <div class="sy-tool">
            <h2 class="sy-h2">Storyletter</h2>
            <p>The editor, for the people designing the content. You design a card, give it a rule for when it comes up,
              and press Play to see what the real engine deals. The node view draws how your cards connect from the
              rules you wrote, and you never wire anything up. <a href={`${base}storyletter/overview/`}>Read about Storyletter.</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="sy-tool">
            <h2 class="sy-h2">Storylet Engine</h2>
            <p>The runtime, for the people shipping the game. What Storyletter dealt at the desk is what your build deals, because the editor runs the same engine your game does. There’s one for your engine, and it loads the one bundle Storyletter publishes. <a href={`${base}play/overview/`}>Read about the runtimes.</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="sy-tool">
            <h2 class="sy-h2">The CLI</h2>
            <p>The command line, for the project lead and CI. <code>storyletengine</code> creates, validates, compiles,
              merges, and measures coverage from a terminal. It runs the same code as the editor, so you can gate a
              build on it and fail the build on a card nothing can reach. <a href={`${base}cli/`}>Read about the CLI.</a></p>
          </div>
          <!-- The engines, on a row of their own under the three tools (as on the Patter landing page). -->
          <ul class="sy-engines">
            {engines.map((e) => (
              <li><img src={`${base}${e.icon}`} alt="" width="30" height="30" /><span>{e.name}</span></li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- DOWNLOADS -->
      <section id="download" class="sy-downloads">
        <div class="sy-wrap sy-downloads-inner">
          <h2 class="sy-h2">Download Storyletter</h2>
          {/* One line: Astro collapses a newline before an inline element to nothing. */}
          <p>Storyletter is the authoring tool: the desktop editor your designers work in. The latest release is read live from GitHub; the runtime for your engine, the CLI, and two playable examples are on the <a href={`${base}download/`}>download page</a>.</p>
          <Downloads kind="storyletter" />
        </div>
      </section>

      <LandingFooter />
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
